<div class="page"><div class="wrap prose">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>I have built and run technology for four decades. For thirteen years I worked at In-Q-Tel, the venture firm that finds technology for the intelligence community, where much of the work was matching a company to a customer who needed it.</p>
  <p>I spent several years as a member of the family office community, attending its conferences, and that is where I learned how these offices decide: a principal, a family, sometimes a shared team, and a technical question nobody in the room can answer. Parallex exists for that question.</p>
  <p>I work alone, on purpose, so the person you speak to is the person who does the work.</p>

  <h3>The name</h3>
  <p><em>Parallax</em> is looking at one thing from two angles. The offset between the views tells you its depth. That is the job: a second view of a company's technology, taken independently of the people selling it.</p>

  <p><%= link_to "Request an introduction", new_introduction_path, class: "btn" %></p>
</div></div>
